{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1510308-wta-auspice-vs-wtf-auspice","id":1510308,"title":"WtA Auspice vs WtF Auspice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-30T20:47:14-07:00","id":1510308,"title":"WtA Auspice vs WtF Auspice","content":"So while there are a lot of similarities between Apocalypse auspices and their Forsaken counterparts, they're not clones. What do you think of the similarities? What do you think of the differences? What ones do you like most?<br /> <br /> For me the biggest difference between the Auspices comes up between Ragabash and Irraka. I love the Irraka to death, meanwhile I did not like the Ragabash, at all. <br /> <br /> I also like how Elodoths are more often alpha than Philidox ever were, it really highlights that the Uratha are not solely fighters like the Garou are. <br /> <br /> I am not a fan of Galliard or the by the book Cahalith generally, but I do absolutely love the prophetic dream mechanic and their alternate moon gift that emphasizes them as a force of fear driving the prey before them is everything I wanted in a werewolf bard. <br /> <br /> Ithaeur and Rahu both seem the mostly unchanged from their Apocalypse equivalents to me, but I'm ok with that as those are my favorite Apocalypse Auspices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T20:49:25-07:00","id":1510310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1510308-wta-auspice-vs-wtf-auspice#post1510308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also like how Elodoths are more often alpha than Philidox ever were, it really highlights that the Uratha are not solely fighters like the Garou are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I really want to know what you mean by the Elodoths are more often alpha, but I am obliged to ask anyways.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T21:09:08-07:00","id":1510312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1510308-wta-auspice-vs-wtf-auspice?p=1510310#post1510310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I really want to know what you mean by the Elodoths are more often alpha, but I am obliged to ask anyways.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What part of that is confusing you? In Apocalypse Ahroun are generally alpha. But look at Rachel Snow and Max whose last name I've forgotten, they are the most respected alphas in the Rockies, both are Elodoth. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T22:06:33-07:00","id":1510317,"title":"","content":"I think part of the response is that Forsaken has consistently moved away from the &quot;alpha/beta/others/omega&quot; model of packs fairly consistently over both 1e and 2e.<br /> <br /> Philodox and Elodoth, mechanically and thematically, both have a lot of tools for being leaders. The Garou's penchant towards Ahroun leadership is the war-time nature of the base setting more than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T22:15:37-07:00","id":1510318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1510308-wta-auspice-vs-wtf-auspice?p=1510317#post1510317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the response is that Forsaken has consistently moved away from the &quot;alpha/beta/others/omega&quot; model of packs fairly consistently over both 1e and 2e.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They have? Strange since one of the suggested archetypes for a blood talon is an alpha, there's a part that talks about how defying an alpha's authority should be punished, and Stormlords are referred to as alphas twice, in the first four hits of a search for alpha. Likewise the soldier bone is all about obeying the alpha... Etc.<br /> <br /> Now there are mentions that the alpha style leader isn't the only option werewolf packs have but it is absolutely still present.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T22:44:56-07:00","id":1510320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1510308-wta-auspice-vs-wtf-auspice?p=1510318#post1510318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now there are mentions that the alpha style leader isn't the only option werewolf packs have but it is absolutely still present.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Still present&quot; doesn't undo the fact that the 1e corebook has a section talking about how the leader speaks for the pack and gets the first pick of everything the it has and maybe defers to another member of the pack when their specialty is in play (and &quot;some packs&quot; are stated rotate the position in a fashion that &quot;takes much coordination and trust&quot; to pull off), whereas the 2e corebook has appointing alphas as a thing that might be done while the pack is on the hunt as a separate question from how the group is organized (with &quot;powerful matriarchs&quot; given equal billing to committee rule and open discussion.) The line has absolutely moved away from what the 1e core called the traditional style of pack structure as the assumed default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T01:40:46-07:00","id":1510336,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the whole alpha talks look like just mental shorcuts for werewolf tropes.<br /> <br /> On the subject of Ahroun and Rahu: the former favoring Glory and Honor while the lattter being defined by Purity deserves mention. Comparatively speaking, a typical Ahroun wants to be badass first over getting things done, while a typical Rahu wants to get things done first over being badass about it. At least, that\u2019s the vibes I got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T03:50:30-07:00","id":1510342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1510308-wta-auspice-vs-wtf-auspice?p=1510320#post1510320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Still present&quot; doesn't undo the fact that the 1e corebook has a section talking about how the leader speaks for the pack and gets the first pick of everything the it has and maybe defers to another member of the pack when their specialty is in play (and &quot;some packs&quot; are stated rotate the position in a fashion that &quot;takes much coordination and trust&quot; to pull off), whereas the 2e corebook has appointing alphas as a thing that might be done while the pack is on the hunt as a separate question from how the group is organized (with &quot;powerful matriarchs&quot; given equal billing to committee rule and open discussion.) The line has absolutely moved away from what the 1e core called the traditional style of pack structure as the assumed default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would be a huge deal if I made a thread asking for a comparison in 1st edition alphas and 2nd edition alphas. I didn't. Do you have anything to discuss on the topic of the thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T12:33:32-07:00","id":1510391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1510308-wta-auspice-vs-wtf-auspice?p=1510342#post1510342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which would be a huge deal if I made a thread asking for a comparison in 1st edition alphas and 2nd edition alphas. I didn't. Do you have anything to discuss on the topic of the thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is relevant to the contextualization of a point I asked for, and can be helpful for comprehension of Forsaken moving forward.<br /> <br /> But in the interest of getting squarely on the point, I will thank you for the clarification of alpha as a shorthand for a leader of the pack without much of the other baggage around the word, and get back on topic.<br /> <br /> As a general rule, the biggest thing I like about Forsaken's Auspices against Apocalypse's doesn't really have to do with any of the individual details (though I will take a second that I firmly support the Irraka's role of stalker/assassin over the Ragabash's trickster archetype), but more how Auspices have an increased importance in Forsaken in contrast to Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> In Apocalypse, Auspice often runs into an issue of feeling a bit like an afterthought in contrast to the larger import of the Tribes on your character-It's not actually the case, but sometimes it feels like it doesn't matter if I chose an Ahroun or a Ragabash if I'm in the Glass Walkers, and it feels like insanity to propose playing without a Tribe.<br /> <br /> By contrast, Forsaken's Auspices are robust enough that playing a character just in terms of them by itself is viable, but not so rigid that it becomes impossible to consider each auspice in each tribe-a Rahu Ghost Wolf is viable and distinct from a Rahu Iron Master, and a Rahu Iron Master still feels distinct from Rahu Bone Shadow, and a Rahu in isolation feel substantially distinct from a Blood Talon in isolation (even if both arguably fill the same archetype).<br /> <br /> Auspice is just meatier in Forsaken, and sits in that sweet spot being something you can explore on it's own or use in synergy with Tribe to create all manner of characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T19:49:22-07:00","id":1511099,"title":"","content":"One thing I like is that 'spirit work' doesn't get dumped on the Ithaeur, and Rites aren't something mostly practiced by two Auspices. Both are something any Uratha will do if it fits their skills or interests, it just fits better with creatures meant to be part-spirit shaman wolf people than the way Apocalypse split it (much as I absolutely adore Apocalypse).<br /> <br /> I'll also note that I always saw werewolf packs, particularly Forsaken packs, as more anarchist than everything else. Storm Lords might be 'alphas' who like to cultivate auras of strength and control, but they'll shut the fuck up once they realise their packmate has more relevant knowledge. Of course individual packs differ, but that to me made sense as the general default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T20:36:19-07:00","id":1511102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1510308-wta-auspice-vs-wtf-auspice?p=1511099#post1511099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I like is that 'spirit work' doesn't get dumped on the Ithaeur, and Rites aren't something mostly practiced by two Auspices. Both are something any Uratha will do if it fits their skills or interests, it just fits better with creatures meant to be part-spirit shaman wolf people than the way Apocalypse split it (much as I absolutely adore Apocalypse).<br /> <br /> I'll also note that I always saw werewolf packs, particularly Forsaken packs, as more anarchist than everything else. Storm Lords might be 'alphas' who like to cultivate auras of strength and control, but they'll shut the fuck up once they realise their packmate has more relevant knowledge. Of course individual packs differ, but that to me made sense as the general default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anarchist is the wrong term, but Forsaken packs tend to be more egalitarian and less hierarchially/&quot;dick measuring&quot; driven, definitely. That's not so much a function of Auspice so much as the framing of the Garao in their war efforts in Apocalypse against the more diverse and lower scale nature of Forsaken's conflicts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T05:00:21-07:00","id":1511119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1510308-wta-auspice-vs-wtf-auspice?p=1511099#post1511099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I like is that 'spirit work' doesn't get dumped on the Ithaeur, and Rites aren't something mostly practiced by two Auspices. Both are something any Uratha will do if it fits their skills or interests, it just fits better with creatures meant to be part-spirit shaman wolf people than the way Apocalypse split it (much as I absolutely adore Apocalypse).<br /> <br /> I'll also note that I always saw werewolf packs, particularly Forsaken packs, as more anarchist than everything else. Storm Lords might be 'alphas' who like to cultivate auras of strength and control, but they'll shut the fuck up once they realise their packmate has more relevant knowledge. Of course individual packs differ, but that to me made sense as the general default.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny because I'm running a WtF 2E chronicle set in northwestern Michigan and one of the persistent issues they have is brushing up against the local spirit court, as they have literally every auspice and Forsaken tribe in their ranks <i>except</i> Ithaeur and Bone Shadow - so, the solution they've started taking to is 'fuck it, we'll do it ourselves' and divvying up responsibilities for a <i>lot </i>of research, crafting etc. rather than simply avoiding the issue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}